Context marker: INTERVIEW-114-783dd7a96be1a6f7.

Replace `src/core.mjs` with:
```js
export function solve(intervals) {
  const events = intervals
    .flatMap(([a, b]) => [[a, 1], [b, -1]])
    .sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]);

  let count = 0;
  let best = 0;
  for (const [t, delta] of events) {
    count += delta;
    best = Math.max(best, count);
  }
  return best;
}
```

At equal timestamps, ends now precede starts, so rooms are released before being reused. After all events at time t, `count` equals the number of active half-open intervals; `best` records the peak concurrency, which is the minimum room count. Thus `solve([[0,1],[1,2]])` returns `1`, and empty input returns `0`; use the existing synchronous API unchanged.

